<p>Use this dialog box to enter a login user name and login password already 
 set on the printer or server for the user authentication. If the user 
 authentication settings have been made on the printer, you also need to 
 make the user authentication settings on the printer driver. Otherwise, 
 you cannot use the printer.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If you do not enter a valid login user name and 
 login password, printing will not start.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="loginname" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Login User Name:</span></p>
<p>Select a type of login user name for user authentication.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Defined User ID</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Specify a login user name already set on the printer 
 or server for user authentication.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Windows Login Name</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Auto-specifies your Windows login name as your user 
 ID.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="enterlogin" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Enter Login User Name:</span></p>
<p>Enter a login user name already set on the printer or server for user 
 authentication.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="pass" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Login Password:</span></p>
<p>Enter a login password already set on the printer or server for user 
 authentication.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Confirmation Password:</span></p>
<p>Enter the login password again for confirmation.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the entries and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this dialog box to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
